== deep-dive
 0   0.35-  3.52  What happens if you hold your breath for as long as you can?
 1   3.78-  6.05  For the first thirty seconds, nothing much.
 2   6.31- 10.76  Your lungs are full, and your blood is still carrying plenty of oxygen.
 3  11.02- 13.39  But carbon dioxide starts building up,
 4  13.91- 18.33  and that, not the lack of oxygen, is what makes you desperate to breathe.
 5  18.59- 21.87  Your diaphragm starts twitching, trying to force a breath,
 6  22.35- 25.57  and your heart actually slows down to save oxygen.
 7  25.83- 29.21  Push even further, and your brain simply switches you off.
 8  29.47- 32.98  You pass out, and your body starts breathing again on its own.
 9  33.24- 36.18  Which is why you should never try this underwater.
